NAME
    decompress - restore a .tcz file made by compress

SYNOPSIS
    decompress <file.tcz> [out] [-k]

DESCRIPTION
    decompress is documented together with its counterpart. See 'man compress'
    for the full description, options, notes, and examples.

    In short: it reverses a .tcz container. A "stored" container needs no data
    card; a truly compressed one needs the card to inflate. The source is
    replaced by the output unless -k/--keep is given; with no 'out' the .tcz
    suffix is stripped.

SEE ALSO
    man compress, man swap, MANUAL.md (Chapter 14)
